window.products.push({"id":78412,"name":"Water Filter","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51t-oKsxHoL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","description":"GE MWFP Pharmaceutical Replacement Refrigerator Water Filter - Single. MWFP Filter - GE SmartWater MWFP Pharmaceutical Refrigerator Water Filter Features: MWFP Filter is a direct OEM replacement for your GE SmartWater refrigerator water filtration system. It is recommended to replace your GE Smartwater MWFP Pharmaceutical filter every 6 months to ensure it ability to reduce water contaminates and maintain proper water flow rate. Reduces sediment chlorine taste and odor Reduces lead cyst and turbidity Reduces waterborne contaminates such as mercury toxaphene p-dichlorobenzene carbofuran alachlor and benzene Certified to NSF Standard 42 & 53 The MWFP Filter is a direct replacement for GE filter part numbers GWF GWFA GWF01 GWF06 MWFA How To Know When Its Time To Change MWFP Pharmaceutical Filter? If your fridge is equipped with a water filter change light you should replace the current filter light turns red. If your refrigerator does not have a change indicator light then it should be changed at least every six months. Installation & Replacement GE SmartWater MWFP Pharmaceutical Water Filter How To Locate the GE MWFP water filter cartridge. It is generally located inside at the right top corner of your refrigerator. Remove the old filter cartridge by grabbing the filter housing and turning to the left about 1/2 turn. Remove the new MWFP filter from the box and fill it with tap water from your faucet. Taking this step allows for better water flow through the filter right after its installation. Place the top of the new cartridge inside the cartridge housing/holder from where you just removed the old filter. Slowly turn the filter clockwise until it stops. The cartridge will move about 1/2 turn and will automatically raise itself into position. Do not over tighten as you could damage the filter or the filter housing. Run water through the system from the water dispenser. Do this for about 2-3 minutes or about 1 gallons of water. This step will flush out any carbon part","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51t-oKsxHoL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"General Electric","source_asin":"B017J7QWM6","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-78412","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B017J7QWM6","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B017J7QWM6","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
